{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nS7 (paper-ionic-ugandakob, change 3066) retired the handler-level `_call_with_retry`. Since then an HTTP 429 or 5xx on a coordinator-routed Jira write gets no retry within the pass: `_dispatch_with_backstop` re-raises every `urllib.error.HTTPError` (`batch_dispatch.py:590-616`), the error escapes `coordinator.coordinate`, and the pass aborts; the next pass re-diffs. ADR 0103 makes `retry_budget.RetryBudget` the sole retry owner (`docs/adr/0103-reconciler-operation-coordination.md:35-43`: at most 3 invocations, 15 s cumulative sleep), and the coordinator already consumes it: `_run_atomic_op` (`coordinator.py:149-162`) retries while `execute` returns `AtomicSignal(status=\"transient\")`. But the production dispatch (`make_coordinator_dispatch`, `batch_dispatch.py:619-646`) only ever returns `applied` or `permanent`, so the budget never fires. `failure_policy.classify_http_error` (`failure_policy.py:118-135`) already maps 429 and 5xx to `transient` and has no production caller. The default budget (`coordinator.py:97-108`) uses `_NullClock`, so even a transient signal would retry with no delay; `run_migrated_reroute` passes `budget_factory=None` (`batch_dispatch.py:684`). Cites are on origin/main dcb35ce77fe.\n\nScope of the coordinator route: `_ACTION_HANDLERS` (`apply_handlers.py:567-571`) dispatches `update` and `delete`. On update the only `HTTPError` that escapes is the scalar `update_issue` (`dispatch_one.py:581`, re-raised at `:601-602`). Reporter (`dispatch_apply_phases.py:205-206`), parent (`dispatch_one.py:486-532`), labels, comments and links catch their own errors, and comments run after `update_issue` (`dispatch_one.py:434-440`), so a retry re-sends only set-style writes (reporter, parent, fields) and has not posted comments yet. A retried delete whose first attempt committed gets a 404, which `handle_delete` soft-fails as today (`apply_handlers.py:543-551`).\n\n## Approach\n1. `retry_budget.py`: add `WallClock` (`now()` = epoch ms from `time.time()`, `sleep_ms(ms)` = `time.sleep(ms / 1000)`). `RetryBudget` itself is unchanged.\n2. `batch_dispatch.py`:\n   - `_transient_http_signal(exc, action)`: `status = _errors.http_status(exc)`; if `classify_http_error(status, action)[0] == \"transient\"`, return `AtomicSignal(status=\"transient\", scope=<its scope>, diagnostic=f\"HTTP {status}\", provider_delay_ms=<Retry-After seconds from exc.headers via _errors.parse_retry_after, ×1000, else None>)`; otherwise `None`.\n   - `make_coordinator_dispatch(..., transient_cell=None)`: wrap the dispatch call in `except urllib.error.HTTPError`; when `_transient_http_signal` returns a signal, store the exception in `transient_cell[0]` (when given) and return the signal without appending an outcome; otherwise re-raise unchanged. A non-429 4xx (and a 404 that reaches here) keeps today's fail-fast re-raise.\n   - `_retry_clock()` returns `retry_budget.WallClock()` (the test seam), and `_transient_budget_factory(cell)` returns a factory building `_TransientRetryBudget(RetryBudget(clock=_retry_clock(), jitter=random.random), cell)`. Its `attempt_retry` delegates; when the plan is not `retry` (`exhausted`, or `defer` because the next delay would pass the 15 s cap), it raises `cell[0]`, so an exhausted budget aborts the pass with the original `HTTPError` exactly as today.\n   - `run_migrated_reroute` creates the cell, passes it to `make_coordinator_dispatch`, and passes `budget_factory=_transient_budget_factory(cell)` to `coordinate_and_fuse`. Each retry goes back through `make_guarded_execute`, so the lost-lease check, the HEAD re-check and the G6 guard run before every attempt.\n3. Out of scope: the create reroute (`reroute_ordered_create_plans`, coordinated write-ahead create), inbound write-backs (`_apply_typed`), the transports' own retries, the default `_NullClock` budget (still used when a caller passes no factory), and ADR 0103's text, which already assigns retry to the budget.\n4. Docs: a BREAKING entry at the top of `docs/release-notes.md` and of `CHANGELOG.md` \"## [Unreleased] / ### Changed\", stating that it partially supersedes S7's \"reconciler handlers make one transport attempt\" entry (release-notes `:11-38`, CHANGELOG `:41-48`): coordinator-routed update and delete now retry 429/5xx within the pass (Retry-After honoured as a lower bound, at most 3 attempts and 15 s of sleep), and exhaustion still aborts the pass. Add one sentence to the Coordinator bullet in `docs/architecture.md:139`.\n\n## Testing (red then green)\nNew `tests/unit/reconciler/mutate/test_coordinator_transient_http_retry.py`, written first and failing on dcb35ce77fe, driving `run_migrated_reroute` with the production dispatch, a fake transport and `_retry_clock` monkeypatched to a recording clock (no real sleep):\n- (a) `update_issue` raises `HTTPError(429)` once then succeeds: 2 transport calls, 1 applied outcome, the clock recorded 1 sleep of at least 2000 ms.\n- (b) the same with 503 (parametrized with 500 and 502).\n- (c) 429 with `Retry-After: 5`: the recorded sleep is at least 5000 ms.\n- (d) `HTTPError(400)` (non-illegal-transition) on every call: 1 call, the raw error propagates, no sleep.\n- (e) 503 on every call: 3 calls, the raw last error propagates, 2 sleeps.\n- (f) 429 with `Retry-After: 30` (beyond the 15 s cap): 1 call, the raw error propagates, no sleep.\nUpdated: `tests/unit/reconciler/mutate/test_operation_coordinator.py:1443-1483` (S7's 503-once test now asserts 2 calls and applied) and `tests/unit/reconciler/test_live_mode_failure_tally.py:794-815` (500 on every call through `applier.apply`: patch `_retry_clock`, assert 3 calls and the raised `HTTPError`). `pytest tests/unit/reconciler -q`; `make verify`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `test_coordinator_transient_http_retry.py` cases (a)-(c): a 429 or 5xx followed by success reaches the transport twice, records one applied outcome, and the recorded budget sleep is at least max(2000 ms, Retry-After).\n- [ ] Case (d): a non-429 4xx reaches the transport once and the raw `HTTPError` propagates with no sleep.\n- [ ] Cases (e)-(f) and `test_live_reroute_reraises_non_404_httperror_fail_fast`: when the budget cannot retry, the raw `HTTPError` propagates out of `run_migrated_reroute` / `applier.apply`, aborting the pass as before.\n- [ ] `git grep -n \"classify_http_error\" -- src/rebar/reconciler/batch_dispatch.py` is non-empty, and `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` prints `new=0 increased=0`.\n- [ ] `docs/release-notes.md` and `CHANGELOG.md` carry the new BREAKING entry naming the S7 entry it partially supersedes; `docs/architecture.md` names the transient mapping.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] `make verify` exits 0.\n  provenance: environment=local dev host; principal=Rebar Bot Nava; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — run log on the ticket"}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1792718351667003001,"uuid":"958d0d0b-785d-4860-85e5-8c0c5bec9526"}